class Solution {
    public int heightChecker(int[] heights) {
        int n = heights.length;
        int[] clone = new int[n];
        int count =0;
        for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
            clone[i]=heights[i];
        }
        Arrays.sort(clone);
         for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
            if(clone[i]!=heights[i]){
                count++;
            }
            
        }
        return count;
    }
}










intition:-
🧠 Pattern (Core Idea)

Expected order = heights ka sorted version (non-decreasing order).

Original array (heights) aur sorted array (expected) ko
index-by-index compare karo.

Jaha value different ho → count +1.

